  "reason": "The best result so far is config_016 (acc=0.542) using scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted + multiprofile. The aggregation (avgpool > transformer) and fusion (weighted > concat) choices are now well-supported. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the RNA encoder (scgpt vs scvi_n200) is a critical design choice. config_011 tests scvi_n200 in the exact best-known architecture (multimodal, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted), directly clarifying whether a different learned RNA encoder can match or exceed scgpt. This is the highest-value experiment because: (1) it isolates the RNA encoder variable while holding all other parameters at their best-known values, (2) if scvi_n200 performs comparably, it opens a new exploration axis; if not, it confirms scgpt's importance and lets us focus remaining budget on other refinements, and (3) with 4 experiments left, reducing uncertainty about this core component is more valuable than testing marginal variations."
